{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966789,"nonce":"qunELrLYnX9yjnd/anIo8ph3P6I=","title":"draw_rgba_pixels images composite in a late unclipped pass; clip via get_clip_data +","message":"`DrawContext::draw_rgba_pixels` (portal_ui noise/texture widgets, video,\ncamera) does NOT emit an SDF primitive — it pushes a `DynamicImage` to\n`batch.dynamic_images`, rendered by `render_dynamic_images` in a SEPARATE\npass that runs AFTER all SDF for that batch. So a raw-pixel upload sits\nabove every SDF primitive in its band by default.\n\n**Clip:** `DynamicImage` now carries `clip_bounds`/`clip_radius`\ncaptured from `get_clip_data()` at emit (the same per-primitive clip SDF\nrespects), applied as the image shader's in-shader clip in\n`render_dynamic_images`. CRITICAL: `get_clip_data()` returns\n`[x, y, width, height]` (NOT `[min_x,min_y,max_x,max_y]`); the sentinel\n`[-10000,-10000,100000,100000]` = no clip. An empty result (zero w/h,\nnon-sentinel) means the element is FULLY outside its clip region this\nframe (e.g. a canvas node panned past the canvas-area edge — node body ∩\ncanvas `overflow_clip` collapses) → `render_dynamic_images` must `continue`\n(skip the image), NOT fall through to a full-coverage draw. The\nfall-through was the \"noise/texture renders above everything\" bug:\nclipped fine while partially on-screen, escaped once fully past the edge.\n\n**Z-order vs HUDs (the minimap):** a canvas-drawn HUD (fill_rect/\nstroke_rect under the inverse-viewport transform) is ordinary canvas SDF,\nso the late dynamic-image pass paints OVER it. Fix: draw the HUD with\n`ctx.set_foreground_layer(true)` — `foreground_primitives` render AFTER\n`render_dynamic_images` in every path (non-compositor Arm A ~9948 / Arm B\n~10014 in context.rs, and the compositor overlay path once\n`render_dynamic_images` is dispatched before `render_foreground_overlay`).\nReset with `set_foreground_layer(false)` after.\n\nActive render path for a continuously-animating canvas on web: usually\n`render_tree_with_motion_opt` → `try_render_with_compositor`, but the\ncanvas-paint fast-path gate can drop it to the non-compositor `_opt`\narms; fixes that depend on pass order must hold in BOTH. The per-image\nin-shader clip and the foreground-layer trick are path-independent, which\nis why they're the robust fixes. See gotcha canvas vs static z ordering,\ngotcha overlay canvas z interleave.","files":null}]}